args: opentide --json share --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Publish objects to intelligence platforms

Usage: opentide share [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  push     Create or update one MISP event per selected object
  preview  Show what push would do, without a request
  status   Compare the local ledger with object versions
  retract  Unpublish or delete a shared event
  targets  List sharing destinations, never their API keys

Options:
      --target <TARGET>
          Destination block name. Repeatable.

      --uuid <UUID>
          Limit to these object UUIDs.

      --type <OBJECT_TYPE>
          Limit to threat, objective, or rule.

      --file <FILE>
          Limit to these object files.

      --dry-run
          Resolve the run locally and make no request.

      --publish, --no-publish
          Override the block publish flag.

      --workers <WORKERS>
          Parallel object workers for one destination.
          
          [default: 1]

      --changed
          Share only objects the default-branch CI diff changed.

      --since <COMMIT>
          With --changed: diff from this commit SHA or ref to HEAD.

      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide share --dry-run
  $ opentide share --target misp-prod

━━━ stderr · empty
